## 3. Paired/remainder energy bookkeeping is unchanged

The new theorem does not alter the parent decomposition.  For retained terminal weights `a,b` and `w=min(a,b)`, pair weights `w,w` and residual weights `a-w,b-w` are nonnegative and disjoint.  Thus pair energy plus residual energy equals the original retained occurrence energy exactly.  The residual measure remains pointwise dominated by the same perimeter measure, so

\[
E_{res}\ge F(z-2P)-o(1)
\]

remains valid.

Consequently

\[
P_{low}\ge P-{\delta-F(z-2P)\over\lambda}-o(1)
\]

has exactly the same proof as in the hostile-audited `1.865` theorem.

**Verdict:** PASS.

