Each complete train has retained pair weight at most one, so this gives the same lower bound on the number of distinct actual O--O trains.  The inherited noncrossing-crosscut theorem therefore gives a simple dual path of linear length.

The interval endpoint budget is `<=2 pi D+o(D)`.  Since

